<h1>Evidence Management Companion</h1>
<p class="page-subtitle">
    An internal aid to the AR 195-5 evidence process. Version 1 supports the case, voucher,
    evidence-item and item-history workflow.
</p>

<div class="panel">
    <h2>What this application is</h2>
    <p>
        EMC assists the AR 195-5 process. Under <strong>AR 195-5 para 2-5c</strong>, an automated
        system "used in conjunction with or to enhance the requirements of this regulation" needs
        no approval. A <em>stand-alone</em> automated evidence ledger or accountability system
        does — for counterintelligence organizations, from <strong>Army G-2X</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
        This application is the first kind. The bound evidence ledger
        (<strong>para 2-5a</strong>) and the original DA Form 4137 (<strong>para 2-4d</strong>)
        remain the authoritative records, and required signatures remain governed by the
        regulation.
    </p>

    <h2>What it will not do</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>It will not assign the evidence document number.</strong> Para 2-4c makes that
            the evidence custodian's act, performed by order of precedence from the evidence
            ledger. EMC issues a temporary identifier such as
            <span class="identifier identifier--temporary">TMP-20260903-A014</span> and records
            the official number, for example <span class="identifier">037-26</span>, once the
            custodian has assigned it in the ledger.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>It will not produce a signature.</strong> Paras 2-5b(2), 2-7b, 3-1b(2) and
            2-8e(5) require handwritten signatures. EMC records that a paper certification was
            executed; that record is not a signature.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>It will not erase history.</strong> Para 2-5b(5) requires an erroneous entry
            to be voided with a single line "so it may still be read" and initialed. EMC's
            equivalent is a correction that preserves the original.
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="panel">
    <h2>Currently implemented</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Create a case and a draft DA Form 4137</li>
        <li>Add and edit evidence items while the voucher is a draft</li>
        <li>Submit a voucher for custodian intake</li>
        <li>Record the official evidence document number assigned in the ledger</li>
        <li>Assign and re-assign evidence-room locations, retaining the full history</li>
        <li>View a complete chronological item history, corrections included</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="regulatory-note">
        Scanned-form ingestion, DA Form 4137 generation, disposition, inspections and inventories
        are designed but not built. See <code>docs/requirements-traceability.md</code>.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" asp-page="/Cases/Index">Go to cases</a></p>
</div>
